Expected elements: present

All backbone items render: nav with resolver, footer with the correct non-asserting disclosure, and the provenance strip with all three marks drawn (text-presentation heart, CodeTracer and GitHub marks in the link indigo). Exactly one provenance marker — the `Data` row, form (c) — sits first in the grid and lands before the empty sections. No debug, retry, spinner or danger tone. The recording-side language is deliberate this round and its prohibition's premise ("the recorder never had the chance") is now false, so I do not count it forbidden.

The page reads as correct, not broken. But the sentence whose only job is to be believed ends in `AvmToolchainRegression` — a bare camelCase enum, unglossed, set in the body face, twice (Not observable card; Data paragraph). A reader cannot evaluate it, and it converts a human admission into a machine echo. The same paragraph shouts `WERE` and prints `2 transaction(s)` / `27 transaction(s)`, so the most load-bearing prose on the page carries template artifacts.

Three further crossings: `Raw (chain-native)` heads a block whose last two fields, `bodyRetainedAtCapture` and `effectVisibleAtCapture`, are capture-adapter bookkeeping, not chain-native; the decoded-input note's "where that is known, it is stated above" resolves to nothing, while the answer sits below it; and the card's refusal reason competes with the paragraph's pruning reason for a transaction at block 67650, outside the stated 67651–67686 window.

Fixes: gloss or replace the enum in prose, and pluralise from the real counts.

Rating: 6/10

